incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Luther Clarence Kissam IV | CEO & Director | Age 60","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Corteva, Inc. is a mid-cap basic materials business with a $5.5B market cap on $17.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding. Operating margins are expanding by +2.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $2.8B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 16 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.11\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 10.4\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 28.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 67% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 45% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Large open-market insider purchases (net $0.5M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Basic Materials sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Corteva to Participate in Goldman Sachs Industrials & Materials Conference","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/corteva-participate-goldman-sachs-industrials-130000779.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795525200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Avantis U.S. Small Cap Value ETF (AVUV) Adds Lyft and Corteva on Nov. 20","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/avantis-u-small-cap-value-110447173.html","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795518287.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentim